    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Note that the ratio of Equation 15.9a to 15.9b gives $ (1-k)/(1+k) $, so that (provided only a single QTL is linked to the marker) an estimate of k can be obtained if one has access to both backcross populations.",
