      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "again providing an estimate of a composite parameter of the QTL effect (a) and position (c). Because $ \\tilde{c} $ is smallest in DHLs (see Equation 15.5b), the largest marker effect (and greatest power for QTL detection) occurs in this type of line, followed by selfed RILs, and finally by sib-mated RILs.",
