    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Finally, note that by considering two-locus (rather than single-locus) marker means, separate estimates of QTL effect and position can be obtained. Taking the genotype at two adjacent marker loci $ (M_{1}/m_{1} $ and $ M_{2}/m_{2}) $ as the unit of analysis, consider the difference between the contrasting double homozygotes in an $ F_{2} $. If the markers flank a QTL, then under the assumption of no interference, Equation 15.2 (and its analog for $ m_{1}m_{1}m_{2}m_{2} $ probabilities) implies",
